 "notes": "Shelf rebuilt in tier mode: three kinds (Humidifier, Dehumidifier, Desiccant moisture absorber), all old kinds kept; the old attribute-only types \"Portable dehumidifier\" and \"Mini dehumidifier\" became t-types. Dehumidifier now attested to the Wikipedia article (old source was empty). Model lists cut to 11/12/4 market-covering models plus independent test winners: Meaco Arete Two 12L (Ideal Home best overall), Meaco DD8L Pro (Ideal Home best desiccant), Pro Breeze 30L and 1500ml Mini (Ideal Home), Midea Cube and Frigidaire 50 Pint (Tom's Guide), Ebac 3850e (HouseFresh best UK), Arete One and EcoAir DD1 (Which? Best Buy per maker pages), Honeywell HCM350 / Venta LW25 / Vicks / Dyson (NBC Select picks), Stadler Form Oskar (Consumer Reports-tested). Left out: Dainichi and Panasonic humidifiers (only Amazon.co.jp retailer snippets surfaced, no maker page retrieved); GoveeLife 50 Pint (Tom's Guide best overall) omitted because no page was fetched; Dyson AM10 (discontinued) kept out of the model list; Hisense and GE dehumidifiers appear only in Consumer Reports' paywalled tested list, not as confirmed winners. Whole-house/furnace humidifiers and whole-house dehumidifiers are out of scope here (Home Fixtures G3). Founding years left blank where the retrieved page did not state one. No craft traditions apply to this shelf.",
